## Test Patterns

### Basic Analytics Test
```typescript
test('should track analytics calls', async () => {
  setCurrentTestName('should track analytics calls');
  
  const { env: mockEnv, analytics } = createMockEnv();
  
  await mockEnv.ANALYTICS_ENGINE.writeDataPoint({
    blobs: ['test_event', 'line_movement'],
    doubles: [1.5, 1000],
    tags: { source: 'test' }
  });
  
  expect(analytics.callCount()).toBe(1);
  expect(analytics.getCalls()[0].blobs).toEqual(['test_event', 'line_movement']);
});
```

### Multiple Calls Test
```typescript
test('should track multiple analytics calls', async () => {
  setCurrentTestName('should track multiple analytics calls');
  
  const { env: mockEnv, analytics } = createMockEnv();
  
  // Make multiple calls
  await mockEnv.ANALYTICS_ENGINE.writeDataPoint({
    blobs: ['event1', 'type1'],
    doubles: [100, 200]
  });
  
  await mockEnv.ANALYTICS_ENGINE.writeDataPoint({
    blobs: ['event2', 'type2'],
    doubles: [300, 400]
  });
  
  expect(analytics.callCount()).toBe(2);
});
```

### Filtering Test
```typescript
test('should filter calls by event type', async () => {
  setCurrentTestName('should filter calls by event type');
  
  const { env: mockEnv, analytics } = createMockEnv();
  
  await mockEnv.ANALYTICS_ENGINE.writeDataPoint({
    blobs: ['nba_123', 'line_movement'],
    doubles: [1.5, 1000]
  });
  
  const nbaCalls = analytics.callsWithBlob('nba_123');
  expect(nbaCalls).toHaveLength(1);
});
```

## Anti-Patterns

### ❌ Don't Do These
```typescript
// Don't use generic mock assertions
expect(mockAnalytics.writeDataPoint).toHaveBeenCalledWith();

// Don't create duplicate stubs
const analytics1 = createAnalyticsEngineStub();
const analytics2 = createAnalyticsEngineStub();

// Don't forget to set test name
test('my test', async () => {
  // Missing setCurrentTestName()
});

// Don't use real Analytics Engine
const realAnalytics = env.ANALYTICS_ENGINE;
```

### ✅ Do These Instead
```typescript
// Use first-class analytics assertions
expect(analytics.getCalls()).toHaveLength(1);

// Use global stub
const { env: mockEnv, analytics } = createMockEnv();

// Set test name for auto-flush
test('my test', async () => {
  setCurrentTestName('my test');
});

// Use analytics stub
const analytics = getGlobalAnalyticsStub();
```

## Performance Characteristics

### Fast Execution
- Tests run in ~20ms (no network calls)
- No external dependencies
- Deterministic results

### Memory Efficient
- Calls stored in memory
- Auto-cleanup after tests
- No memory leaks

### Reliable
- No network flakes
- Consistent behavior
- Easy to debug

